  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Identify the amplitude, period, and phase of these functions.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-q5a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=\\sin\\left(3x+\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Amplitude: $1$; period: $\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$; phase: $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ (shift left).",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=\\sin\\left(3\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right)\\\\A&=1\\\\T&=\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\end{aligned}$$\nThe horizontal shift is $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ left, so the phase is $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ in the source's convention.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q5b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=-6\\sin\\left(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Amplitude: $6$; period: $4\\pi$; phase: $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ (shift left).",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=-6\\sin\\left(\\frac12\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\\right)\\\\A&=|-6|=6\\\\T&=\\frac{2\\pi}{1/2}=4\\pi\\end{aligned}$$\nThe horizontal shift is $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ left, so the phase is $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ in the source's convention. The negative coefficient reflects the graph across the $x$-axis without changing its amplitude.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q5c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=3\\sin\\left(2x-\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Amplitude: $3$; period: $\\pi$; phase: $-\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ (shift right).",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=3\\sin\\left(2\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)\\right)\\\\A&=3\\\\T&=\\frac{2\\pi}{2}=\\pi\\end{aligned}$$\nThe horizontal shift is $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ right, so the phase is $-\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ in the source's convention.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q5d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{5\\cos\\left(\\frac{x+\\pi}{3}\\right)}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Amplitude: $2.5$; period: $6\\pi$; phase: $\\pi$ (shift left).",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=\\frac52\\cos\\left(\\frac13(x+\\pi)\\right)\\\\A&=\\frac52=2.5\\\\T&=\\frac{2\\pi}{1/3}=6\\pi\\end{aligned}$$\nThe horizontal shift is $\\pi$ left, so the phase is $\\pi$ in the source's convention.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      }
    ]
  },
